# Files that widen or narrow Claude Code's own guardrails or authority, and
# the inputs those guards read.
#
# With "require review from Code Owners" on the main ruleset, a PR touching
# any of these cannot merge without David's APPROVAL — that half of the
# carve-out rule in CLAUDE.md (Close-out → carve-outs) becomes server-side.
# What this file does NOT do: restrict who clicks merge after approval;
# GitHub has no per-path merge-actor rule. "Never merge a carve-out myself"
# therefore stays Claude Code's own rule, backed by the receipt hook.
#
# Coverage is by dependency, not by name: guard-decision.mjs imports
# pr-ready.mjs and review-budget.mjs; pr-ready.mjs imports
# review-loop-record.mjs and review-counting.mjs; review-budget.mjs and
# review-loop-record.mjs import review-counting.mjs. classify-ci-paths.mjs
# decides which CI jobs run. AGENTS.md is the source the shared working rules
# derive from. Adding a gate input means adding it here.
